Third-party data in this repository

The token windows under data/repair_transfer/windows/, data/selective_editing/windows/ and data/quickstart/ are
sequences of token ids, not text. Each windows.json names the source file, its revision and sha256, and the rows
each window came from. All windows were made the same way: the source text was tokenized with the target model's
tokenizer, cut to a window of 257 tokens, and selected by the rule recorded in windows.json. Row ranges below are
0-based and inclusive.

Europarl v7. Philipp Koehn. Europarl: A Parallel Corpus for Statistical Machine Translation. MT Summit X, 2005.
https://www.statmt.org/europarl/v7/europarl.tgz
The corpus's Terms of Use state: "We are not aware of any copyright restrictions of the material."
https://www.statmt.org/europarl/ (checked 13 October 2026).
The page requests citation of the corpus paper and contact with its maintainer when the data are used in research.
This is the source's statement, not a declaration that the material is public domain or covered by this repository's licences.
  Used in:
    every directory under data/repair_transfer/windows/
    data/quickstart/
    data/selective_editing/windows/train, val, test, guard_europarl_en, protected_europarl_val and protected_europarl_test
    data/selective_editing/windows/retain_en rows 0-127
    data/selective_editing/windows/val_en rows 0-31.

WikiText-2 (wikitext-2-raw-v1), collected by Stephen Merity, Caiming Xiong, James Bradbury and Richard Socher from
text by Wikipedia contributors. Citation: Pointer Sentinel Mixture Models, 2016. Source:
https://huggingface.co/datasets/Salesforce/wikitext, revision b08601e04326c79dfdd32d625aee71d232d685c3 (validation and
test parquet files). The original dataset page links to CC BY-SA 3.0 Unported:
https://www.salesforce.com/blog/the-wikitext-long-term-dependency-language-modeling-dataset/?bc=OTH
These selected and tokenized excerpts are distributed under CC BY-SA 3.0 Unported:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/
The source Hugging Face metadata also lists GFDL.
  Changes: selected and tokenized into 257-token windows, as described in windows.json.
  Covered files and rows:
    data/selective_editing/windows/guard_wikitext/en.npy, all 32 rows (test split)
    data/selective_editing/windows/retain_en/en.npy, rows 128-191 (validation split)
    data/selective_editing/windows/qcheck_en/en.npy, rows 0-63 (validation split).

NTREX-128. Christian Federmann, Tom Kocmi, Ying Xin. NTREX-128 - News Test References for MT Evaluation of 128
Languages. SUMEval 2022. Source: https://github.com/MicrosoftTranslator/NTREX, commit
